[92mlitellm.acompletion(model='gpt-4o', api_base=None, messages=[{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a fair judge assistant assigned to deliver insightful feedback that compares individual performances, highlighting how each stands relative to others within the same cohort.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, a reference answer, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of two responses strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, choose a better response between Response A and Response B. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: "(write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (A or B)"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###Instruction:\n\nImagine you are a medical professional tasked with evaluating simulated doctor-patient conversations generated from summary notes. \nThese conversations should accurately reconstruct interactions based on the SOAP (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan) format provided in the notes.\n\nHere is the medical note:\n#############################\nCHIEF COMPLAINT\n\nJoint pain.\n\nHISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS\n\nThe patient is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease who presents with some joint pain.\n\nThe patient reports that her left elbow has really been bothering her. She states that she sits at her desk all day for work with her elbows bent. She reports that after work it is really hard for her to flex and extend her left elbow. She reports that it has been really stiff and painful. She also notes that she has noticed swelling on the olecranon of her elbow. She reports that she is right-handed, therefore, she can still write, which is great, but typing is difficult. She denies any numbness or tingling in her hands. She reports that she has some weakness in her arm but nothing too significant. She denies any fever or chills.\n\nRegarding her epilepsy, she reports that she has not had any recent seizures. She reports that her last seizure was a year ago. She reports that she is still taking Keppra.\n\nRegarding her depression, she reports that she started therapy last year and she is trying to avoid medications for this problem. She reports that therapy has been helpful, but she still feels down and stressed. She denies suicidal and homicidal ideations.\n\nRegarding her peptic ulcer, she reports that she was dealing with a lot of stress last year. She then underwent an endoscopy which showed that she had an episode of gastritis. She was subsequently diagnosed with peptic ulcer disease and started Protonix. She reports that she has not had any issues with her ulcer since the procedure and everything has been good.\n\nThe patient denies chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting. She reports that she does have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies.\n\nREVIEW OF SYSTEMS\n\n• Ears, Nose, Mouth and Throat: Endorses medial nasal congestion from allergies.\n• Cardiovascular: Denies chest pain or dyspnea on exertion.\n• Respiratory: Denies shortness of breath.\n• Musculoskeletal: Endorses left elbow joint pain, swelling, and weakness.\n• Psychiatric: Endorses depression.\n\nPHYSICAL EXAMINATION\n\n• Musculoskeletal: Examination of the left elbow reveals erythema and edema. Pain to palpation of the left olecranon. Warm to palpation. Pain with flexion and extension. Palpable left radial pulse.\n\nRESULTS\n\nLeft arm x-ray does not reveal any evidence of elbow fracture.\n\nEGD revealed an episode of gastritis.\n\nASSESSMENT\n\nAnna Morris is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease who presents with some joint pain.\n\nPLAN\n\nLeft elbow pain.\n• Medical Reasoning: I believe she has left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma.\n• Medical Treatment: Initiate meloxicam 15 mg once daily.\n• Patient Education and Counseling: I encouraged the patient to use a pillow to rest her arm on. She may also ice the area.\n\nEpilepsy.\n• Medical Reasoning: She has been doing well on Keppra and denies any recent seizures.\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Keppra 500 mg twice a day. This was refilled today.\n\nDepression.\n• Medical Reasoning: She reports doing well with therapy.\n• Medical Treatment: Initiate Lexapro 10 mg once daily.\n\nPeptic ulcer disease.\n• Medical Reasoning: Her recent endoscopy revealed gastritis\n• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg once daily before meals.\n\nPatient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.\n\n#############################\n\n\n###Response A:\n{{ [doctor] Hi there, how are you doing today?\n\n[patient] Hi, I\'m okay. Thanks for seeing me.\n\n[doctor] Great. What brings you in to see me today?\n\n[patient] I\'ve been having some joint pain in my left elbow.\n\n[doctor] Oh, sorry to hear that. Can you tell me more about the pain?\n\n[patient] Sure. It\'s been really bothering me. I sit at my desk all day for work with my elbows bent. After work, it\'s really hard for me to flex and extend my left elbow. It\'s really stiff and painful. I\'ve also noticed some swelling on the olecranon of my elbow.\n\n[doctor] Hmm, that sounds uncomfortable. Do you have any numbness or tingling in your hands?\n\n[patient] No, I don\'t have any numbness or tingling in my hands.\n\n[doctor] Okay, that\'s good to know. How about weakness in your arm?\n\n[patient] Yes, I do have some weakness in my arm, but nothing too significant.\n\n[doctor] Alright. Have you had any fever or chills?\n\n[patient] No, I haven\'t had any fever or chills.\n\n[doctor] Okay. How about your epilepsy? Have you had any recent seizures?\n\n[patient] No, I haven\'t had any recent seizures. My last seizure was about a year ago.\n\n[doctor] Good to hear that. Are you still taking Keppra?\n\n[patient] Yes, I am. I still take Keppra 500 mg twice a day.\n\n[doctor] Okay. How about your depression? How are you doing with that?\n\n[patient] I\'ve been trying to avoid medications for depression, but I started therapy last year and it\'s been helpful. I\'m still feeling down and stressed, though.\n\n[doctor] I see. Have you had any suicidal or homicidal thoughts?\n\n[patient] No, I haven\'t.\n\n[doctor] Good to hear that. How about your peptic ulcer? How have you been doing with that?\n\n[patient] I was dealing with a lot of stress last year, and then I had an endoscopy which showed an episode of gastritis. I was diagnosed with peptic ulcer disease and started taking Protonix. Everything has been good since then.\n\n[doctor] That\'s good to hear. Do you have any chest pain, shortness of breath, abdominal pain, nausea, or vomiting?\n\n[patient] No, I don\'t have any of those symptoms.\n\n[doctor] Okay. Do you have any nasal congestion or sinus issues?\n\n[patient] Yes, I do have a little bit of medial nasal congestion from allergies.\n\n[doctor] Alright. Let\'s go through a quick review of your systems. How\'s your ear, nose, mouth, and throat?\n\n[patient] I have medial nasal congestion from allergies.\n\n[doctor] Okay. Any chest pain or shortness of breath?\n\n[patient] No, I don\'t have chest pain or shortness of breath.\n\n[doctor] How about your respiratory system? Any shortness of breath?\n\n[patient] No, I don\'t have shortness of breath.\n\n[doctor] Alright. How about your musculoskeletal system? Any joint pain or swelling?\n\n[patient] Yes, I have joint pain in my left elbow, swelling, and weakness.\n\n[doctor] Okay. How about your psychiatric system? How have you been feeling emotionally?\n\n[patient] I\'ve been feeling down and stressed, but I\'m trying to manage it with therapy.\n\n[doctor] Alright. Let\'s do a physical exam. I\'ll start with your musculoskeletal exam. I\'ll check your left elbow. \n\n[doctor] The examination of your left elbow reveals erythema and edema. There\'s pain to palpation of the left olecranon. The area feels warm to palpation, and there\'s pain with flexion and extension. I can feel your left radial pulse, though.\n\n[patient] Oh, that sounds pretty painful.\n\n[doctor] Yes, it does. Let\'s take a look at some imaging. A left arm x-ray doesn\'t show any evidence of an elbow fracture.\n\n[patient] That\'s good to hear.\n\n[doctor] Yes, it is. Your endoscopy did show an episode of gastritis, which is related to your peptic ulcer disease.\n\n[patient] Okay.\n\n[doctor] Based on all this, I think you have left olecranon bursitis caused by repetitive trauma.\n\n[patient] What does that mean?\n\n[doctor] It means that the fluid-filled sac around the elbow joint is inflamed, likely due to repetitive bending and flexing at your desk job.\n\n[patient] Ah, I see.\n\n[doctor] I\'m going to start you on meloxicam 15 mg once daily to help with the pain and inflammation. \n\n[patient] Okay, that sounds good.\n\n[doctor] I\'ll also recommend using a pillow to rest your arm on when you\'re at work. Additionally, you can try icing the area to reduce the swelling.\n\n[patient] I\'ll do that.\n\n[doctor] How\'s your epilepsy been doing?\n\n[patient] It\'s been good. I haven\'t had any recent seizures.\n\n[doctor] That\'s great. You\'re currently taking Keppra 500 mg twice a day. I\'ll refill that for you today.\n\n[patient] Thanks.\n\n[doctor] How about your depression? You mentioned you\'re still feeling down and stressed.\n\n[patient] Yes, I am.\n\n[doctor] I\'ll start you on Lexapro 10 mg once daily to help with your depression.\n\n[patient] Alright.\n\n[doctor] You\'re already taking Protonix 40 mg once daily for your peptic ulcer disease. You\'ll continue that.\n\n[patient] Okay.\n\n[doctor] Do you understand and agree with the recommended medical treatment plan?\n\n[patient] Yes, I do.\n\n[doctor] Great. If you have any further questions or concerns, feel free to call us. We\'ll see how you respond to the treatment and adjust as needed.\n\n[patient] Thank you, I appreciate it.\n\n[doctor] You\'re welcome. Take care, and we\'ll see you in a month for a follow-up.\n\n[patient] Thanks, I\'ll see you then. }}<|eot_id|>\n\n###Response B:\n{{ Patient: Hello.\n\nDoctor: Hello, hi there. Um, can you confirm your name and date of birth for me please?\n\nPatient: Um, my name is Anna Morris and my date of birth is 23rd of April 1997.\n\nDoctor: Okay, great. And you\'re calling from the UK. Can you confirm your address and your postcode for me please?\n\nPatient: Um, I\'m calling from the UK. Um, my address is 12 Oakwood Drive, and my postcode is LS12 6JN.\n\nDoctor: Okay, great. And, um, can you confirm your phone number for me please?\n\nPatient: Um, yes, my phone number is 0113 1234567.\n\nDoctor: Okay, great. And can you confirm your name and date of birth again for me please?\n\nPatient: Yeah, my name is Anna Morris and my date of birth is 23rd of April 1997.\n\nDoctor: Okay, great. Um, can you confirm your medical history for me please?\n\nPatient: Um, I have epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease.\n\nDoctor: Okay, great. And can you tell me a bit more about your epilepsy? Um, what kind of seizures do you have?\n\nPatient: Um, I have partial seizures. Um, I don\'t really know what that means. Um, I just get a sort of tingling feeling in my hands and feet, and sometimes I get a funny feeling in my head. Um, but I don\'t really know what it is.\n\nDoctor: Okay, great. And how long have you had those seizures for?\n\nPatient: Um, I think I\'ve had them for like, I don\'t know, maybe 10 years now. Um, they\'ve been getting less frequent, but they still happen.\n\nDoctor: Okay, great. And how often do they happen to you?\n\nPatient: Um, it varies. Um, sometimes I can go like, weeks without having one, and then